issue.body:
If you run the following module with run_hlo_module

```
HloModule elmwise

ENTRY main (f0: bf16[1,2,3072], f1: f32[1,2,4096], f2: f32[2,4096], f3: bf16[2,4096,3072], f4: bf16[18432], f5: bf16[8,18432]) -> bf16[2,4096,3072] {
  param_0 = bf16[1,2,3072] parameter(0)
  param_1 = f32[1,2,4096] parameter(1) 
  param_2 = f32[2,4096] parameter(2)
  param_3 = bf16[2,4096,3072] parameter(3)
  param_4 = bf16[18432] parameter(4)
  param_5 = bf16[8,18432] parameter(5) 
  convert.15948.18 = f32[2,4096,3072] convert(param_3)
  broadcast.39695.9 = f32[2,4096,3072] broadcast(param_2), dimensions={0,1}
  subtract.1127.9 = f32[2,4096,3072] subtract(convert.15948.18, broadcast.39695.9)
  bitcast.288148.19 = f32[2,4096] bitcast(param_1)
  broadcast.39699.19 = f32[2,4096,3072] broadcast(bitcast.288148.19), dimensions={0,1}
  multiply.47350.7 = f32[2,4096,3072] multiply(subtract.1127.9, broadcast.39699.19)
  convert.15949.5 = bf16[2,4096,3072] convert(multiply.47350.7)
  bitcast.288160.7 = bf16[2,3072] bitcast(param_0)
  broadcast.39701.7 = bf16[2,4096,3072] broadcast(bitcast.288160.7), dimensions={0,2}
  multiply.47351.3 = bf16[2,4096,3072] multiply(convert.15949.5, broadcast.39701.7)
  slice.4087.15 = bf16[2,18432] slice(param_5), slice={[0:2], [0:18432]}
  broadcast.39630.15 = bf16[2,18432] broadcast(param_4), dimensions={1}
  add.26676.15 = bf16[2,18432] add(slice.4087.15, broadcast.39630.15)
  slice.4112.3 = bf16[2,3072] slice(add.26676.15), slice={[0:2], [9216:12288]}
  broadcast.39702.3 = bf16[2,4096,3072] broadcast(slice.4112.3), dimensions={0,2}
  ROOT add.26709.1 = bf16[2,4096,3072] add(multiply.47351.3, broadcast.39702.3)
}
```

you'll get errors like

```
INVALID_ARGUMENT: layout minor_to_major field contains 3 elements, but shape has 2 dimensions: {2, 1, 0}; shape: bf16[2,3072]
```

I think it's because XLA will propagate the layout from the bf16[1,2,3072] tensor to the bf16[2,3072] tensor. If I remove the bitcasts, the module runs without issues.

```
HloModule elmwise

ENTRY main (f0: bf16[1,2,3072], f1: f32[1,2,4096], f2: f32[2,4096], f3: bf16[2,4096,3072], f4: bf16[18432], f5: bf16[8,18432]) -> bf16[2,4096,3072] {
  param_0 = bf16[2,3072] parameter(0)
  param_1 = f32[2,4096] parameter(1) 
  param_2 = f32[2,4096] parameter(2)
  param_3 = bf16[2,4096,3072] parameter(3)
  param_4 = bf16[18432] parameter(4)
  param_5 = bf16[8,18432] parameter(5) 
  convert.15948.18 = f32[2,4096,3072] convert(param_3)
  broadcast.39695.9 = f32[2,4096,3072] broadcast(param_2), dimensions={0,1}
  subtract.1127.9 = f32[2,4096,3072] subtract(convert.15948.18, broadcast.39695.9)
  broadcast.39699.19 = f32[2,4096,3072] broadcast(param_1), dimensions={0,1}
  multiply.47350.7 = f32[2,4096,3072] multiply(subtract.1127.9, broadcast.39699.19)
  convert.15949.5 = bf16[2,4096,3072] convert(multiply.47350.7)
  broadcast.39701.7 = bf16[2,4096,3072] broadcast(param_0), dimensions={0,2}
  multiply.47351.3 = bf16[2,4096,3072] multiply(convert.15949.5, broadcast.39701.7)
  slice.4087.15 = bf16[2,18432] slice(param_5), slice={[0:2], [0:18432]}
  broadcast.39630.15 = bf16[2,18432] broadcast(param_4), dimensions={1}
  add.26676.15 = bf16[2,18432] add(slice.4087.15, broadcast.39630.15)
  slice.4112.3 = bf16[2,3072] slice(add.26676.15), slice={[0:2], [9216:12288]}
  broadcast.39702.3 = bf16[2,4096,3072] broadcast(slice.4112.3), dimensions={0,2}
  ROOT add.26709.1 = bf16[2,4096,3072] add(multiply.47351.3, broadcast.39702.3)
}
```

Filing to track. I'll try to find some time to fix this myself this week.
